ves, tilting the balance of the upcoming US elections.

The backlash has even led US conservatives =E2=80=93 politicians and consti=
tuents =E2=80=93 to split from wealthy allies in Silicon Valley.

The opposition to datacenters in the US has become so widespread that it is=
 crossing partisan lines. Several prominent US conservatives, including the=
 governors of Texas and Florida, have condemned datacenters=E2=80=99 enormo=
us electricity usage. Both states=E2=80=99 governors hew closely to Trump o=
n the majority of issues, but both have implemented restrictions on datacen=
ters=E2=80=99 access to their states=E2=80=99 power grids.

