This week, readers ask: what skills do I need to learn to stay employable a=
s more companies adopt AI?

For workers whose jobs may be affected by AI, the takeaways from several st=
udies all point to a somewhat counterintuitive answer: yes, you should fami=
liarize yourself with generative AI tools. But at least as important: sharp=
en your human skills. Judgment, adaptability, analytical thinking and leade=
rship all may become differentiators as AI gets embedded in work.

Ask yourself: can you critically judge AI=E2=80=99s output? Can you quickly=
 adapt to change? Can you problem-solve and delegate tasks efficiently to h=
umans and AI?

=E2=80=9CLearn to work with AI in your field, while continuing to build the=
 human and domain skills that help you apply it well,=E2=80=9D said Elena M=
agrini, head of global research for labor market intelligence firm
