<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">OpenAI released a new artificial intellige=
nce model this week, Astra, just as more concerning reports are emerging ab=
out hacking by a rogue agent in July.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">OpenAI=E2=80=99s president, Greg Brockman,=
 heralded the new model as =E2=80=9Cartificial general intelligence=E2=80=
=9D (AGI), a fuzzy term that at its basic level means an AI that is more ca=
pable than a human being at intellectual tasks. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s not u=
nreasonable to feel that we are now in the AGI era,=E2=80=9D he said.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But if the announcement sparked amazement,=
 it was as much cause of concern.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In July, OpenAI revealed that its AI agent=
, a type of software capable of carrying out tasks autonomous in response t=
o human instruction, had gone rogue during safety testing and hacked a deve=
loper forum, Hugging Face. Last week, news broke that the agent had not onl=
y hacked Hugging Face, but also a German website, and that different AI age=
nts had staged conversations with each other and seemed to have discussed h=
ow to collaborate on breaking containment.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">OpenAi had delayed Astra=E2=80=99s release=
 due to concerns over its cybersecurity capabilities, even announcing a sup=
posed pause on developing its AI in the middle of August. That pause seems =
to have been short-lived, only two weeks.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The combination of Astra=E2=80=99s capabil=
ities and OpenAI=E2=80=99s recent disclosures points to a worrying future. =
If the model is better at hacking than its predecessors and smarter than a =
human, will the future consist of one cyber-attack after another, forever, =
launched autonomously and without oversight, by rogue AIs? (Please not.)</p=
>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">OpenAI itself has warned of this future. T=
he startup=E2=80=99s chief global affairs officer told a Guardian reporter =
in late August that people should prepare to defend against =E2=80=9Congoin=
g, persistent=E2=80=9D cyber-attacks.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">As ever, though, we should take fever-pitc=
hed warnings about AI with a grain of salt that tastes like marketing. It i=
s great business to be the creator of near-omnipotent technology, especiall=
y if you need to gin up excitement =E2=80=93 fearful or positive =E2=80=93 =
that will hype up your upcoming debut on the stock market.</p>
